WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.634
-We have a lot to get into.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:07.567
First of all, your evolution from the game of --

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.534
or evolution of life from the game of tennis.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.434
-Evolution, yeah. -Not retirement.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:15.000
-No, 'cause -- You know what? 'Cause I always feel like --

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.234
I think retirement is something that's super earned

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:18.968
and that people work really hard for.

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:21.968
And -- [ Chuckles ] Maybe I haven't worked hard enough.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:25.167
But I just feel like I'm at an age

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.367
where I definitely have a lot more to give,

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:29.267
and there's a lot more that I want to do.

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:31.501
And so I'm not gonna be relaxing.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.300
There's so much more for me, and --

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.534
-Yeah.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.567
-I feel it's more of like an evolution of Serena.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.167
And there's -- there's so many things

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.167
that I've been wanting to do for so many years.

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.534
And I have such a passion for tennis for so long

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:45.267
that I have never done it, but now it's time for me

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:47.434
to, like, start to enjoy those things.

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:49.701
-When did you -- When did you know --

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:50.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.567
You should enjoy it. -I should.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.968
It's hard. It's a little hard. -You worked too hard. I know.

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.667
It's a difficult choice, probably,

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.834
because you're going, "Well, this is my thing.

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:00.367
I've worked so hard for this."

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:04.033
But it's also very brave of you to stop and be like,

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:06.033
"No, I have other things I want to do.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.534
I have things to offer." -Yeah.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:10.400
-When did you know? When did you go like, "This is it.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.000
I've talked to my husband. I've talked to my friends..."

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.501
Who knew? Can you tell us who knew?

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:16.934
-Um, well, in the beginning,

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.434
I literally couldn't tell anyone.

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:21.367
And I write about it in the magazine, in "Vogue."

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:23.734
I just say the only person that knew at one point

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.334
was my therapist 'cause I was just --

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.534
'Cause verbalizing it meant that it was real.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:28.701
-Wow. -And I'm like,

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.133
"I don't want it to be real."

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:33.334
So, you know, I wasn't quite sure, like,

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:35.200
where I was gonna -- what I was gonna do.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.300
And I don't think you really know until --

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.534
I don't know --

00:01:39.534 --> 00:01:41.200
until you say it or until it's actually real.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.501
And then -- It's so funny. When everything came out,

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:46.367
I thought -- The whole time I was stressed out,

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.033
I thought I was gonna be really miserable

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:50.133
and just scared of this whole article coming out,

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.701
'cause it was a lot on me.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:53.367
You have to think. I've been playing tennis

00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:56.968
since, um -- since I was literally in a stroller.

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:59.200
And there's a picture of Venus pushing me in a stroller.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.234
And that's how long I've been around tennis.

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:06.334
And for me to suddenly, like, have to be done, it was like,

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:08.634
okay, well, you know, this is a big thing.

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:10.667
But anyway, when it came out, I was actually relieved,

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.501
and I didn't expect to feel that way.

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:13.834
I felt good. -You were relieved?

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:15.834
-Yes. I felt pretty good.

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:19.067
And then, um, yeah, I was like, "Okay, yeah."

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:21.367
It's like -- when you want to accomplish something

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:23.400
and you don't do it, but then when you finally do it,

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.434
it's like, "Oh, it wasn't as bad as I thought it was."

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:26.434
-Yeah. -You know?

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:27.767
And that's kind of what it was like.

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:29.801
I should have done it ten years ago! I'm just kidding.

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.334
-No, no. That's not what we're saying.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:34.868
So there's no chance of you pulling a Tom Brady

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:37.834
and maybe saying, "You know what? Maybe I'm not ready.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:40.868
I'm evolving into a -- coming back. Pickleball."

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:41.934
-You know what? Tom --

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:43.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:47.434
You know what? Tom Brady started an amazing trend.

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.400
-Yes. He started an amazing trend.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.601
-That's what I'm gonna say. -That's all you're gonna say.

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:56.067
That's very smart.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:59.701
I read somewhere that you're not good at saying goodbyes.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:01.267
-No, no.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:03.067
-So you don't really want to make a big fanfare like --

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.868
"Bye, everyone. Goodbye, goodbye, goodbye."

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:07.100
-No. I always thought that, you know,

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.334
at the end of it I would just, um --

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.901
just leave quietly and just, like, not say anything

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.601
and just make an announcement, like,

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.801
on social media or something. That's how I always thought.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:17.200
That's how I always envisioned it.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.767
-You thought you were gonna sneak away?

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:20.067
-Yeah. -Like, "Oh, by the way.

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:21.400
Bye." Yeah, right.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.200
-Yeah, you know. -Are you like that at a party?

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.667
Like, if I have you at my party, will you leave and not tell me?

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:28.400
-Yeah, I mean, if it's not -- [ Laughter ]

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.367
If it's not happening, if you're not playing the right music

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.100
and I'm not dancing, I'm out of there.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.667
-I'm playing the right -- Really?

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:36.434
Not even the -- You just go like, "I'll be right back"?

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:38.033
Or do you, like -- -Well, I've done that

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.300
actually on a date once.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.767
I --

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:43.167
-On a date once? -Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:44.868
-What are you talking about?

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:47.634
-Well, I was not having a great --

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.033
It was years ago, obviously.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.701
But I was not having a great date,

00:03:50.701 --> 00:03:52.501
and so I just went to the bathroom.

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:53.968
-And never came back?

00:03:53.968 --> 00:03:56.834
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.400
And never came back?!

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.167
-I've yet to go back.

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:03.367
-Oh, my goodness. No way.

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:06.000
-It was fun. I was young. -Yeah.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.767
-No need to waste time. I can't waste time.

00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:11.300
-When I saw you at Wimbledon in London, did you know?

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.934
That you were gonna -- -Yeah, I did, I did.

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:16.033
And it was -- I was heavy. Like, I was heavy for months.

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.467
-Yeah. -You know, and I don't know

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.367
if you knew my energy, but I was just so heavy,

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:21.467
and I just wasn't even rocking out the way I wanted

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:23.100
to rock out. I was just sitting there.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.701
But, literally, when it came out, like,

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:27.968
all this stuff just got released,

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:29.334
and I just felt better.

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:32.167
-I'm so happy. There's so many things.

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:33.901
I want to talk about what's next for you.

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:36.100
But Serena Ventures. Is that -- -Yeah.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.067
-I mean, that's already crushing it.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.100
-Yeah, and you know a lot about the investing world,

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.400
but I've been investing for --

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.901
This is my tenth year of doing it now.

00:04:43.901 --> 00:04:46.634
So we finally took outside capital,

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:48.968
and we raised a lot of money, and we invested in lots of women

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:52.200
and lots people of color, and just literally everyone.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.767
Everyone has a seat at our table.

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:56.667
And so that's what we want to see more in the investing world,

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.634
is, like, giving everyone an opportunity

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:01.200
and really just investing in founders, you know?

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.934
And just -- So that's kind of --

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.267
That's the mission that we started,

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:05.901
and we're keeping it up. -You're crushing it.

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:07.667
You're doing a great job with that.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.234
I love that, and it's doing really well.

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:10.701
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:13.167
-It's very hard to get that off the ground. You've done it.

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.300
But let's talk about "The Adventures of Qai Qai."

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:18.133
This is very, very cute. -Qai Qai.

00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:21.234
-I love children's books. And I have two little girls.

00:05:21.234 --> 00:05:22.734
So they're gonna love this.

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:26.334
Basically it's about a girl who has her doll, Qai Qai,

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:27.934
and she talks to the doll and is like,

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:30.367
"I get nervous about doing a performance."

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:31.801
And the doll talks her through it.

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:33.934
And then she's like, "Do you want to come out with me?"

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.367
And spoiler alert -- she's like,

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:36.934
"I'm not allowed to bring the doll.

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:38.167
I have to do it myself."

00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:39.734
And the strength was in her the whole time.

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:40.968
-I'm proud of you for reading it.

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:42.467
-Of course I read it. Are you kidding me?

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.968
-I was gonna quiz you. And now I don't have to quiz you.

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:46.901
-No, I love the book. Believe in yourself.

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:48.501
Believe it and do it, and you can do anything.

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:49.734
-That's right, and that's what --

00:05:49.734 --> 00:05:51.534
"The Adventures of Qai Qai" is all about that.

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:53.067
You can do anything. -You can do anything.

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:54.767
-Yes. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:58.167
-You guys, "The Adventures of Qai Qai."

00:05:58.167 --> 00:05:59.968
Serena Williams, everybody! -Thank you.

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:01.868
[ Cheers and applause ] -September 27th.

00:06:01.868 --> 00:06:04.000
We'll be right back with Justin Long, everybody.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.133
Stick around.

